cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Averaged Jacobian Regularity Does Not Order Few-Step Error in Flow Matching: A Certified Gaussian Counterexample"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying manuscript, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Callaert
    given-names: Clément
    email: callaert.clement@gmail.com
    affiliation: "CentraleSupélec and Université Paris-Saclay"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/clement-callaert/fewstep-field-regularity"
url: "https://github.com/clement-callaert/fewstep-field-regularity"
abstract: >
  Flow matching and stochastic interpolants specify a probability flow ODE
  whose few-step sampling error depends on the sampling schedule. Chen,
  Vanden-Eijnden, and Xu propose minimizing averaged squared Jacobian
  regularity A2 as a path-selection criterion. This work gives a certified
  Gaussian counterexample and a three-regime map of when that scalar orders
  equal-NFE Wasserstein-2 error.
keywords:
  - flow matching
  - stochastic interpolants
  - few-step sampling
  - Lipschitz regularity
  - Wasserstein distance
  - Runge-Kutta
